(function(E){ const x = E["exam-02"] = E["exam-02"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x02-r2"] = {"id":"x02-r2","patterns":["RA-history","GT2-career","GT2-policy","PARA-cause","PARA-rules"],"title":{"en":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","tr":"Reading 2: Passage 2 / Section 2","fa":"Reading ۲: متن ۲ (Passage 2) / بخش ۲ (Section 2)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which lettered section contains a piece of information, to choose TWO correct statements from five, and to complete a summary with single words from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi harfli bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, beş ifadeden doğru İKİSİNİ seçmeyi ve bir özeti metindeki tek kelimelerle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی یک اطلاعات در کدام بخشِ حرف‌دار است، از پنج جمله دو جمله‌ی درست را انتخاب کنی و یک خلاصه را با تک‌کلمه‌هایی از متن کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete a table from a list of an employer’s promises, and a flow-chart of steps from a workplace guide, using no more than one or two words from the text.","tr":"Bu derste bir işverenin taahhüt listesinden bir tabloyu ve bir iş yeri rehberinden adımları gösteren bir akış şemasını, metinden en fazla bir ya da iki kelime kullanarak tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جدول را از فهرست تعهدهای یک کارفرما و یک فلوچارتِ مرحله‌ها را از یک راهنمای محل کار کامل کنی، با حداکثر یک یا دو کلمه از متن."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 2: an archaeology article","tr":"Reading Passage 2: bir arkeoloji yazısı","fa":"Reading Passage 2: یک مقاله‌ی باستان‌شناسی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to find which lettered section contains a piece of information, to choose TWO correct statements from five, and to complete a summary with single words from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir bilginin hangi harfli bölümde olduğunu bulmayı, beş ifadeden doğru İKİSİNİ seçmeyi ve bir özeti metindeki tek kelimelerle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری پیدا کنی یک اطلاعات در کدام بخشِ حرف‌دار است، از پنج جمله دو جمله‌ی درست را انتخاب کنی و یک خلاصه را با تک‌کلمه‌هایی از متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Sections","tr":"Bölüm","fa":"بخش"},"value":"A-G"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a city before kings","tr":"Bu sınav: krallardan önce bir kent","fa":"این آزمون: شهری پیش از پادشاهان"},"intro":{"en":"History and archaeology are among the most frequent Academic Reading topics. A Passage 2 like this one has lettered sections, a clear line of argument (an old idea, new evidence, a new idea) and a lot of dates and places.","tr":"Tarih ve arkeoloji Academic Reading’in en sık konularındandır. Bunun gibi bir Passage 2’de harfli bölümler, açık bir düşünce çizgisi (eski bir fikir, yeni kanıtlar, yeni bir fikir) ve çok sayıda tarih ve yer vardır.","fa":"تاریخ و باستان‌شناسی از پرتکرارترین موضوع‌های Academic Reading هستند. یک Passage 2 مثل این بخش‌های حرف‌دار، یک خط استدلال روشن (یک ایده‌ی قدیمی، شواهد تازه، یک ایده‌ی تازه) و تاریخ و مکان‌های زیادی دارد."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x02-r2-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-history","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An ancient trading town","tr":"Eski bir ticaret kenti","fa":"یک شهر تجاری باستانی"},"asks":{"en":"An archaeology article in seven lettered sections: an old theory, a site and its finds, trade, how the town was organised, why it was abandoned and how it is protected today.","tr":"Harfli yedi bölümden oluşan bir arkeoloji yazısı: eski bir kuram, bir kazı alanı ve buluntuları, ticaret, kentin nasıl örgütlendiği, neden terk edildiği ve bugün nasıl korunduğu.","fa":"یک مقاله‌ی باستان‌شناسی در هفت بخشِ حرف‌دار: یک نظریه‌ی قدیمی، یک محوطه و یافته‌هایش، تجارت، اینکه شهر چطور اداره می‌شد، چرا رها شد و امروز چطور از آن محافظت می‌شود."},"fields":["The old theory","The site","Food and materials","Long-distance trade","How the town was organised","Decline","Threats today"],"words":[{"a":"overturn an idea","b":"show that a theory is wrong","tr":"bir fikri çürütmek","fa":"رد کردن یک ایده"},{"a":"excavation","b":"digging a site carefully","tr":"kazı","fa":"کاوش"},{"a":"layer","b":"a level of earth from one period","tr":"katman","fa":"لایه"},{"a":"settle","b":"begin to live in a place","tr":"yerleşmek","fa":"ساکن شدن"},{"a":"lack","b":"not have / there is no","tr":"yoksun olmak","fa":"نداشتن"},{"a":"in exchange for","b":"traded for / paid with","tr":"karşılığında","fa":"در ازای"},{"a":"well established","b":"already common / long in place","tr":"yerleşik, köklü","fa":"جاافتاده"},{"a":"a ruling class","b":"a small group with power","tr":"yönetici sınıf","fa":"طبقه‌ی حاکم"},{"a":"cooperation","b":"working together","tr":"iş birliği","fa":"همکاری"},{"a":"uncertain","b":"still debated / not known","tr":"belirsiz","fa":"نامعلوم"},{"a":"illegally","b":"against the law","tr":"yasa dışı yollarla","fa":"غیرقانونی"},{"a":"restricted","b":"limited by law","tr":"kısıtlanmış","fa":"محدودشده"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"Which section contains...\" often points to one detail, not the main idea of a section. A reference to money can sit in one sentence of a paragraph about something else.","tr":"\"Hangi bölüm şunu içeriyor...\" çoğu zaman bir bölümün ana fikrini değil, tek bir ayrıntıyı gösterir. Paraya bir gönderme, başka bir konudaki paragrafın tek cümlesinde olabilir.","fa":"«کدام بخش شامل... است» اغلب به یک جزئیات اشاره می‌کند، نه ایده‌ی اصلیِ بخش. اشاره به پول ممکن است در یک جمله از پاراگرافی درباره‌ی موضوع دیگری باشد."},{"en":"The same words in two sections: a statement about \"trade\" may match the section that explains why trade was needed, not the one that uses the word most.","tr":"İki bölümde aynı kelimeler: \"ticaret\" hakkındaki bir ifade, kelimeyi en çok kullanan bölüme değil, ticaretin neden gerektiğini açıklayan bölüme uyabilir.","fa":"کلمه‌های یکسان در دو بخش: جمله‌ای درباره‌ی «تجارت» ممکن است با بخشی جور باشد که توضیح می‌دهد چرا تجارت لازم بود، نه بخشی که بیشتر از همه این کلمه را به کار می‌برد."}],"example":{"text":"\"B  The harbour was rebuilt twice. The second time, the work was paid for by a tax on wine.\"","item":"Which section contains a reference to how a project was funded?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"One detail, \"paid for by a tax\", matches \"how it was funded\", although the section is mainly about rebuilding.","tr":"Bölüm çoğunlukla yeniden yapımla ilgili olsa da tek bir ayrıntı, \"bir vergiyle ödendi\", \"nasıl finanse edildiği\" ile eşleşiyor.","fa":"با اینکه بخش بیشتر درباره‌ی بازسازی است، یک جزئیات، «با یک مالیات پرداخت شد»، با «چطور تأمین مالی شد» جور است."}}},{"id":"RA-culture","ctx":["RA-history","RA-culture"],"title":{"en":"Arguments about art, heritage and history","tr":"Sanat, miras ve tarih üzerine tartışma yazıları","fa":"نوشته‌های استدلالی درباره‌ی هنر، میراث و تاریخ"},"asks":{"en":"A review or an argument about art, museums, heritage or history: should museums return objects, is street art real art, what a history book gets right. YES/NO/NOT GIVEN asks about the writer’s views; multiple choice asks about the writer’s purpose.","tr":"Sanat, müzeler, kültürel miras ya da tarih üzerine bir eleştiri veya tartışma yazısı: müzeler eserleri iade etmeli mi, sokak sanatı gerçek sanat mı, bir tarih kitabı neyi doğru yapıyor. YES/NO/NOT GIVEN yazarın görüşlerini sorar; çoktan seçmeli sorular yazarın amacını sorar.","fa":"نقد یا نوشته‌ای استدلالی درباره‌ی هنر، موزه‌ها، میراث یا تاریخ: آیا موزه‌ها باید اشیا را پس بدهند، آیا هنر خیابانی هنر واقعی است، یک کتاب تاریخ چه چیزی را درست می‌گوید. YES/NO/NOT GIVEN نظر نویسنده را می‌پرسد؛ چندگزینه‌ای هدف نویسنده را."},"fields":["The writer believes the book is too long. (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","The writer’s main point in paragraph 3 is...","Museums should charge for entry. (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","Summary with a box: the writer thinks the ___ of the exhibition was..."],"words":[{"a":"the writer believes","b":"in my view / I would argue","tr":"yazara göre","fa":"نویسنده معتقد است"},{"a":"convincing","b":"persuasive / makes a strong case","tr":"ikna edici","fa":"قانع‌کننده"},{"a":"overrated","b":"praised more than it deserves","tr":"abartılmış","fa":"بیش از اندازه ستوده‌شده"},{"a":"neglected","b":"ignored / overlooked","tr":"ihmal edilmiş","fa":"نادیده‌گرفته‌شده"},{"a":"authentic","b":"genuine / the real thing","tr":"özgün","fa":"اصیل"},{"a":"controversial","b":"causes disagreement","tr":"tartışmalı","fa":"بحث‌برانگیز"},{"a":"heritage","b":"the past a community keeps","tr":"kültürel miras","fa":"میراث"},{"a":"accessible","b":"easy for the public to reach or understand","tr":"erişilebilir","fa":"در دسترس"},{"a":"criticise","b":"find fault with","tr":"eleştirmek","fa":"انتقاد کردن"},{"a":"underestimate","b":"think it matters less than it does","tr":"küçümsemek","fa":"دست‌کم گرفتن"},{"a":"admittedly","b":"it is true that... but","tr":"kabul etmek gerekir ki","fa":"البته"},{"a":"dismiss","b":"reject without serious thought","tr":"önemsememek","fa":"رد کردن"}],"traps":[{"en":"Reported views: \"some critics say the exhibition is too small\" is not the writer’s view unless the writer agrees.","tr":"Aktarılan görüşler: \"bazı eleştirmenler serginin küçük olduğunu söylüyor\" yazar katılmadıkça yazarın görüşü değildir.","fa":"نظرهای نقل‌شده: «بعضی منتقدها می‌گویند نمایشگاه کوچک است» نظر نویسنده نیست، مگر اینکه نویسنده موافق باشد."},{"en":"NOT GIVEN: the writer discusses the topic but gives no opinion on the exact point of the statement.","tr":"NOT GIVEN: yazar konuyu tartışır ama ifadedeki noktaya dair görüş bildirmez.","fa":"NOT GIVEN: نویسنده درباره‌ی موضوع حرف می‌زند، ولی درباره‌ی همان نکته‌ی جمله نظری نمی‌دهد."},{"en":"Concession: \"it is true that the museum is expensive, but...\". The writer’s real view comes after \"but\".","tr":"Kabul etme: \"müzenin pahalı olduğu doğru ama...\". Yazarın asıl görüşü \"but\"tan sonra gelir.","fa":"پذیرش موقت: «درست است که موزه گران است، اما...». نظر واقعی نویسنده بعد از «but» می‌آید."}],"example":{"text":"Critics have called the new gallery cold and unwelcoming. I disagree: its plain white rooms let the paintings speak for themselves, which is exactly what a gallery should do.","item":"Statement: The writer thinks the new gallery is unwelcoming.  (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"NO","why":{"en":"\"Unwelcoming\" is the critics’ view. \"I disagree\" makes the writer’s view the opposite: NO.","tr":"\"Soğuk\" eleştirmenlerin görüşü. \"Katılmıyorum\" yazarın görüşünü tersine çeviriyor: NO.","fa":"«بی‌روح» نظر منتقدهاست. «موافق نیستم» نظر نویسنده را برعکس می‌کند: NO."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-history"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-history","n":35,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 35 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 35’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۵ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Three tasks, one passage","tr":"Tek metin, üç görev","fa":"یک متن، سه تمرین"},"body":{"en":"Questions 14-19: which section, A-G, contains each piece of information (a letter can be used more than once). Questions 20-21: choose TWO letters from A-E. Questions 22-26: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage.","tr":"Soru 14-19: her bilgi hangi bölümde (A-G) yer alıyor (bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir). Soru 20-21: A-E arasından İKİ harf seç. Soru 22-26: özeti metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۴ تا ۱۹: هر اطلاعات در کدام بخش (A تا G) است (یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید). سؤال‌های ۲۰ و ۲۱: از A تا E دو حرف انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۲۲ تا ۲۶: خلاصه را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Do the section task last","tr":"Bölüm görevini en sona bırak","fa":"تمرینِ بخش‌ها را آخر انجام بده"},"steps":[{"en":"Start with the summary and the choose-TWO question: they follow the passage and teach you where things are.","tr":"Özetle ve iki-seçenekli soruyla başla: metni izlerler ve neyin nerede olduğunu öğretirler.","fa":"با خلاصه و سؤالِ دوگزینه‌ای شروع کن: دنبال متن می‌آیند و یادت می‌دهند هر چیز کجاست."},{"en":"For \"which section\", note the kind of information asked for: a reason, an example, a comparison, a description.","tr":"\"Hangi bölüm\" için istenen bilginin türünü not et: bir neden, bir örnek, bir karşılaştırma, bir tanım.","fa":"برای «کدام بخش» نوع اطلاعاتی را که خواسته شده یادداشت کن: دلیل، مثال، مقایسه، توصیف."},{"en":"Read each section for that kind of sentence, not for the same words.","tr":"Her bölümü aynı kelimeler için değil, o türden bir cümle için oku.","fa":"هر بخش را برای پیدا کردن آن نوع جمله بخوان، نه برای کلمه‌های یکسان."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"A detail, not the main idea","tr":"Ana fikir değil, bir ayrıntı","fa":"یک جزئیات، نه ایده‌ی اصلی"},"body":{"en":"The information you need is often a single sentence inside a section that is mainly about something else. Do not choose a section because its first line sounds right.","tr":"Aradığın bilgi çoğu zaman esas olarak başka bir şeyden söz eden bir bölümün içindeki tek bir cümledir. İlk satırı doğru göründüğü için bir bölümü seçme.","fa":"اطلاعاتی که لازم داری اغلب یک جمله است، داخل بخشی که بیشتر درباره‌ی چیز دیگری است. بخشی را فقط چون خط اولش درست به نظر می‌رسد انتخاب نکن."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One summary gap, step by step","tr":"Bir özet boşluğu, adım adım","fa":"یک جای خالی خلاصه، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the summary. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage.","text":"\"The first houses were built of wood. Later, after several fires, the town council insisted that all new houses should be made of stone.\"","item":"After a number of ___, stone became the required building material.","answer":"fires","walk":[{"en":"\"A number of\" before the gap means a plural noun.","tr":"Boşluktan önceki \"a number of\" çoğul bir isim ister.","fa":"«a number of» قبل از جای خالی یعنی یک اسم جمع."},{"en":"\"Required\" = the council \"insisted\"; find what came before that.","tr":"\"Required\" = konsey \"ısrar etti\"; ondan önce ne olduğunu bul.","fa":"«required» یعنی شورا «اصرار کرد»؛ پیدا کن قبلش چه اتفاقی افتاد."},{"en":"\"After several fires\": copy fires, with the s.","tr":"\"Birkaç yangından sonra\": fires’ı s ile kopyala.","fa":"«بعد از چند آتش‌سوزی»: fires را با s کپی کن."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"A section is mostly about farming, but one sentence says \"the grain was sold to towns on the coast\". Which question could this section answer?","options":["a reference to selling goods","a description of how farms were organised","an explanation of why people left"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"One sentence about selling grain is enough: \"which section\" questions often point to a single detail.","tr":"Tahıl satışıyla ilgili tek bir cümle yeter: \"hangi bölüm\" soruları çoğu zaman tek bir ayrıntıyı gösterir.","fa":"یک جمله درباره‌ی فروش غلات کافی است: سؤال‌های «کدام بخش» اغلب به یک جزئیات اشاره می‌کنند."}},"remember":{"en":"Name the kind of information, then look for that kind of sentence. The answer is often a detail.","tr":"Bilginin türünü belirle, sonra o türden bir cümle ara. Cevap çoğu zaman bir ayrıntıdır.","fa":"نوع اطلاعات را مشخص کن و بعد دنبال همان نوع جمله بگرد. جواب اغلب یک جزئیات است."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x02-r2-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 2","title":{"en":"A city before kings","tr":"Krallardan önce bir kent","fa":"شهری پیش از پادشاهان"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-history"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading Passage 2 below.","passage":"A city before kings\n\nA  For much of the twentieth century, historians believed that towns in West Africa had appeared only after traders from North Africa began crossing the Sahara with their camels, from around the eighth century AD. According to this view, it was contact with the outside world that brought trade, new ideas and powerful rulers, and cities grew up as a result. The ruins of Jenné-jeno, in the inland delta of the River Niger in present-day Mali, have done more than any other site to overturn that idea.\n\nB  The site is a large mound of earth about three kilometres from the modern town of Djenné, standing just above a floodplain that is covered with water for part of every year. A survey in the late 1970s and excavations in the early 1980s showed that people first settled there around 250 BC. Because the style of the pottery changed over the centuries, and because burnt material from each layer can be dated scientifically, the excavators were able to build up a detailed timeline of the town. The settlement grew slowly at first, but by about AD 900 it covered more than 33 hectares, and dozens of smaller mounds within a few kilometres of it were occupied at the same time, so that the whole area may have been home to tens of thousands of people.\n\nC  Life depended on the river. Each year the flood left behind fertile soil in which people grew rice, and the water provided fish while the dry season grasslands fed cattle. Yet the delta itself lacks some basic materials. There is no stone suitable for grinding grain, and no local source of iron ore. Iron objects were nevertheless found in the very lowest layers of the site, together with signs that metal was worked there, though not made from ore. This means that stone and iron had to be brought in from elsewhere, probably by boat along the river, in exchange for the food that the floodplain produced in such quantity.\n\nD  Some of the goods reached Jenné-jeno from much further away. Copper must have come from deposits several hundred kilometres to the north, and small glass beads appear to have travelled even greater distances. What surprised the excavators was the date of these finds. Several of them came from layers that are older than the earliest camel caravans across the Sahara. Long-distance trade, in other words, was already well established before the outside contacts that were once thought to have created it. The caravans, when they came, joined a network that West Africans had built themselves.\n\nE  Perhaps the most debated finding concerns the way the town was organised. In many early cities, such as those of ancient Mesopotamia, archaeologists find palaces, temples and burials full of treasure, all signs of a ruling class. At Jenné-jeno there is no clear sign of a palace, no monumental building and no group of unusually rich graves. Instead, the evidence suggests that specialists such as smiths, potters and fishermen lived in separate clusters, each perhaps with its own customs, and depended on one another through trade. The excavators proposed that the town worked through cooperation between these groups rather than through the commands of a single powerful family, although not every archaeologist accepts this interpretation, and some argue that far more of the site must be excavated first.\n\nF  The later history of the site is clearer. Around AD 800, a wall of mud brick about two kilometres long was built around the main mound, and over the following centuries houses changed from a round to a rectangular shape. After about 1200, however, the population began to fall, and by around 1400 the town had been abandoned. Why this happened is still uncertain. One explanation is that people moved to the growing town of Djenné nearby, which had become an important centre of trade and learning. Others point to changes in rainfall, or to disease spreading among the population, and it is possible that several causes worked together.\n\nG  Today the greatest threat to the site comes not from nature but from people. Clay figures made at Jenné-jeno are highly valued by collectors, and in the 1980s and 1990s many were dug out illegally and sold abroad. Each hole destroyed the layers that allow archaeologists to date what they find, so that much information has been lost for ever. The area is now protected as part of a World Heritage Site, and the sale of such objects has been restricted. Researchers hope that, with better protection, the mounds, most of which have never been excavated, still have much to teach us about how cities can begin.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 14-19. Reading Passage 2 has seven sections, A-G. Which section contains the following information? Write the correct letter, A-G, in boxes 14-19 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E","F","G"],"questions":[{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"a reference to materials that the town had to obtain from elsewhere","correct":2,"evidence":"stone and iron had to be brought in from elsewhere","why":{"en":"C: there was no stone or iron ore locally, so \"stone and iron had to be brought in from elsewhere\".","tr":"C: Bölgede taş ya da demir cevheri yoktu, bu yüzden \"taş ve demir başka yerlerden getirilmek zorundaydı\".","fa":"C: سنگ و سنگ‌آهن در محل نبود، پس «سنگ و آهن باید از جای دیگری آورده می‌شد»."},"trap":["TR-detail","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":15,"kind":"match","prompt":"a description of an earlier theory that the findings went against","correct":0,"evidence":"have done more than any other site to overturn that idea","why":{"en":"A: historians believed towns came only after the caravans; the site helped \"overturn that idea\".","tr":"A: Tarihçiler kentlerin kervanlardan sonra çıktığına inanıyordu; alan \"bu fikri çürütmeye\" yardım etti.","fa":"A: تاریخ‌دان‌ها فکر می‌کردند شهرها فقط بعد از کاروان‌ها پیدا شدند؛ این محوطه به «رد کردن آن ایده» کمک کرد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"match","prompt":"a mention of the harm done by people looking for objects to sell","correct":6,"evidence":"many were dug out illegally and sold abroad","why":{"en":"G: clay figures \"were dug out illegally and sold abroad\", and each hole destroyed layers.","tr":"G: kil heykelcikler \"yasa dışı yollarla kazılıp yurt dışına satıldı\" ve her çukur katmanları yok etti.","fa":"G: مجسمه‌های گلی «به‌طور غیرقانونی بیرون آورده و به خارج فروخته شدند» و هر چاله لایه‌ها را از بین برد."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":17,"kind":"match","prompt":"an indication of how large the settlement became","correct":1,"evidence":"it covered more than 33 hectares","why":{"en":"B: by about AD 900 \"it covered more than 33 hectares\".","tr":"B: MS 900 civarında \"33 hektardan fazla alanı kaplıyordu\".","fa":"B: حدود سال ۹۰۰ میلادی «بیش از ۳۳ هکتار را می‌پوشاند»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":18,"kind":"match","prompt":"a suggestion that no single group held power in the town","correct":4,"evidence":"rather than through the commands of a single powerful family","why":{"en":"E: the town may have worked through cooperation \"rather than through the commands of a single powerful family\".","tr":"E: kent \"tek bir güçlü ailenin emirleriyle değil\" iş birliğiyle işlemiş olabilir.","fa":"E: شاید شهر با همکاری اداره می‌شد، «نه با فرمانِ یک خانواده‌ی قدرتمند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"match","prompt":"a list of possible reasons why the town came to an end","correct":5,"evidence":"Others point to changes in rainfall","why":{"en":"F: people may have moved to Djenné; \"others point to changes in rainfall, or to disease\".","tr":"F: insanlar Djenné’ye göç etmiş olabilir; \"başkaları yağıştaki değişikliklere ya da hastalığa işaret ediyor\".","fa":"F: شاید مردم به جنه رفتند؛ «دیگران به تغییر بارش یا بیماری اشاره می‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","PARA-cause"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 20-21. Choose TWO letters, A-E. Write the correct letters in boxes 20 and 21 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":20,"n2":21,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO of the following finds are mentioned in the passage?","options":["A coins with writing on them","B iron objects in the oldest layers","C stone buildings used for worship","D glass beads from distant places","E written records of trade"],"correct":[1,3],"evidence":"Iron objects were nevertheless found in the very lowest layers of the site","trap":["TR-samewords","TR-paraphrase"],"why":{"en":"B \"iron objects... in the very lowest layers\" and D \"glass beads appear to have travelled even greater distances\". Stone is mentioned only as something the delta lacks; coins and written records are not mentioned.","tr":"B \"en alt katmanlarda... demir nesneler\" ve D \"cam boncuklar daha da uzak mesafeler kat etmiş görünüyor\". Taştan yalnızca deltada bulunmayan bir şey olarak söz ediliyor; madeni para ve yazılı kayıtlar geçmiyor.","fa":"B «اشیای آهنی... در پایین‌ترین لایه‌ها» و D «مهره‌های شیشه‌ای ظاهراً مسافت‌های بیشتری را پیموده‌اند». از سنگ فقط به‌عنوان چیزی که دلتا ندارد حرف زده شده؛ سکه و سند نوشته‌شده اصلاً نیامده‌اند."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 22-26. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-26 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"How the town was organised and how it ended","questions":[{"n":22,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Archaeologists have found no clear sign of a ___ or of graves full of treasure.","accept":["palace"],"limit":1,"evidence":"there is no clear sign of a palace","why":{"en":"\"There is no clear sign of a palace, no monumental building and no group of unusually rich graves.\"","tr":"\"Bir saraya, anıtsal bir binaya ya da olağandışı zengin mezarlara dair açık bir iz yok.\"","fa":"«هیچ نشانه‌ی روشنی از کاخ، بنای یادمانی یا گورهای غیرعادی پرثروت نیست»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":23,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Instead, ___ such as smiths and potters seem to have lived in separate groups.","accept":["specialists"],"limit":1,"evidence":"specialists such as smiths, potters and fishermen","why":{"en":"\"Specialists such as smiths, potters and fishermen lived in separate clusters.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Demirciler, çömlekçiler ve balıkçılar gibi uzmanlar ayrı kümelerde yaşıyordu.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«متخصص‌هایی مثل آهنگرها، سفالگرها و ماهیگیرها در گروه‌های جدا زندگی می‌کردند». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Around AD 800, a mud-brick ___ was built around the main mound.","accept":["wall"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a wall of mud brick about two kilometres long","why":{"en":"\"A wall of mud brick about two kilometres long was built around the main mound.\"","tr":"\"Ana tepenin çevresine yaklaşık iki kilometre uzunluğunda kerpiçten bir sur yapıldı.\"","fa":"«دیواری از خشت، حدود دو کیلومتر طول، دور تپه‌ی اصلی ساخته شد»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Over time, houses were built in a ___ shape instead of a round one.","accept":["rectangular"],"limit":1,"evidence":"from a round to a rectangular shape","why":{"en":"\"Houses changed from a round to a rectangular shape.\"","tr":"\"Evler yuvarlak biçimden dikdörtgen biçime geçti.\"","fa":"«خانه‌ها از شکل گرد به شکل مستطیل تغییر کردند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"After about 1200 the population fell, and by around 1400 the town had been ___.","accept":["abandoned"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the town had been abandoned","why":{"en":"\"By around 1400 the town had been abandoned.\"","tr":"\"1400 civarında kent terk edilmişti.\"","fa":"«حدود سال ۱۴۰۰ شهر رها شده بود»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x02-r2-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"By 1500 the village had been abandoned.\" This means that people...","options":["had rebuilt it","had sold it","had left it for good"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Abandoned = left and not returned to.","tr":"Abandoned = terk edilmiş, geri dönülmemiş.","fa":"abandoned یعنی رها شده و کسی برنگشته."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"A summary says \"people began to live there\". Which word in a passage means the same?","options":["excavated","settled","flooded"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"To settle = to start living in a place.","tr":"Settle = bir yerde yaşamaya başlamak.","fa":"settle یعنی شروع به زندگی در یک جا کردن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Which of the three tasks is usually best left until last?","options":["which section contains the information","the summary","the choose-TWO question"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The other tasks follow the passage and show you where things are; the section task jumps around.","tr":"Diğer görevler metni izler ve neyin nerede olduğunu gösterir; bölüm görevi ise metinde atlar.","fa":"تمرین‌های دیگر دنبال متن می‌آیند و نشان می‌دهند هر چیز کجاست؛ تمرینِ بخش‌ها این‌طرف و آن‌طرف می‌پرد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Section C is mainly about farming, but one sentence says boats carried goods along the river. Can section C be the answer to \"a reference to transport\"?","options":["No: the section is about farming","Only if its first line is about transport","Yes: one detail is enough"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Which section\" questions often point to one detail inside a section.","tr":"\"Hangi bölüm\" soruları çoğu zaman bir bölümün içindeki tek bir ayrıntıyı gösterir.","fa":"سؤال‌های «کدام بخش» اغلب به یک جزئیات داخل بخش اشاره می‌کنند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":1,"prompt":"An option says \"stone tools were found\". The passage says \"there is no stone suitable for making tools nearby\". Is the option correct?","options":["Yes: stone is mentioned","No: the same word with a different meaning","Only partly"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The same word appears, but the passage says the opposite.","tr":"Aynı kelime geçiyor ama metin tersini söylüyor.","fa":"همان کلمه آمده، اما متن برعکسش را می‌گوید."}}],"id":"c-x02-r2-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r2"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 2: work texts","tr":"GT Reading Section 2: iş metinleri","fa":"GT Reading Section 2: متن‌های کاری"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete a table from a list of an employer’s promises, and a flow-chart of steps from a workplace guide, using no more than one or two words from the text.","tr":"Bu derste bir işverenin taahhüt listesinden bir tabloyu ve bir iş yeri rehberinden adımları gösteren bir akış şemasını, metinden en fazla bir ya da iki kelime kullanarak tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جدول را از فهرست تعهدهای یک کارفرما و یک فلوچارتِ مرحله‌ها را از یک راهنمای محل کار کامل کنی، با حداکثر یک یا دو کلمه از متن."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Word limit","tr":"Kelime sınırı","fa":"سقف کلمه"},"value":{"en":"1 / 2 words","tr":"1 / 2 kelime","fa":"۱ / ۲ کلمه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: an agency and a bike scheme","tr":"Bu sınav: bir ajans ve bir bisiklet programı","fa":"این آزمون: یک آژانس و طرح دوچرخه"},"intro":{"en":"Section 2 always has two work-related texts: job adverts, career guides, workplace rules or schemes. The language is formal, and rules are often given with must, will and cannot.","tr":"Section 2’de her zaman işle ilgili iki metin vardır: iş ilanları, kariyer rehberleri, iş yeri kuralları ya da programları. Dil resmîdir ve kurallar çoğu zaman must, will ve cannot ile verilir.","fa":"Section 2 همیشه دو متن مرتبط با کار دارد: آگهی استخدام، راهنمای شغلی، قانون‌ها یا طرح‌های محل کار. زبانش رسمی است و قانون‌ها اغلب با must، will و cannot گفته می‌شوند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x02-r2gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT2-career","GT2-policy","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-career","n":18,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Agency promises and a bike scheme","tr":"Ajans taahhütleri ve bir bisiklet programı","fa":"تعهدهای یک آژانس کاریابی و طرح دوچرخه"},"asks":{"en":"Section 2 is about work. Here: what a temping agency promises its workers, and how employees join a company scheme to get a bike, step by step.","tr":"Section 2 iş hayatıyla ilgilidir. Burada: geçici iş ajansının çalışanlarına verdiği sözler ve çalışanların bir şirket programıyla adım adım nasıl bisiklet edindiği.","fa":"Section 2 درباره‌ی کار است. این‌جا: قول‌هایی که یک آژانس کار موقت به کارکنانش می‌دهد و اینکه کارمندها قدم به قدم چطور از طریق طرح شرکت دوچرخه می‌گیرند."},"fields":["Before you start","Pay","Holiday","Notice","Support","Safety","Who can join","Steps to apply"],"words":[{"a":"on our books","b":"registered with us","tr":"kayıtlı","fa":"ثبت‌نام‌شده نزد ما"},{"a":"build up","b":"collect over time / save up","tr":"birikmek","fa":"جمع شدن"},{"a":"notice","b":"a warning before something happens","tr":"önceden haber","fa":"اطلاع قبلی"},{"a":"turn down","b":"refuse / say no to","tr":"reddetmek","fa":"رد کردن"},{"a":"premises","b":"the buildings and land of a business","tr":"işyeri binası","fa":"محل کار، ساختمان"},{"a":"eligible","b":"allowed to join","tr":"hak sahibi, uygun","fa":"واجد شرایط"},{"a":"quotation","b":"a written price","tr":"fiyat teklifi","fa":"پیش‌فاکتور"},{"a":"approve","b":"agree / give permission","tr":"onaylamak","fa":"تأیید کردن"},{"a":"spread over","b":"paid in parts across","tr":"... boyunca taksitlendirilmiş","fa":"قسطی در طولِ"}],"traps":[{"en":"NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: \"a written quotation\" is three words if you copy the article. Leave out a, an and the when they are not needed.","tr":"NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: \"a written quotation\" başındaki a ile üç kelimedir. Gerekmiyorsa a, an ve the’yi yazma.","fa":"NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: «a written quotation» با a سه کلمه است. اگر لازم نیست a، an و the را ننویس."},{"en":"The table or flow-chart may say \"employer\" where the text says \"your manager\" or \"HR\". Match the step, then copy the text’s own words.","tr":"Tablo ya da akış şeması \"employer\" diyebilir, metin ise \"your manager\" ya da \"HR\" der. Adımı eşleştir, sonra metnin kendi kelimelerini kopyala.","fa":"جدول یا فلوچارت ممکن است بگوید «employer» در حالی که متن می‌گوید «your manager» یا «HR». قدم را پیدا کن، بعد کلمه‌های خودِ متن را کپی کن."}],"example":{"text":"\"Uniforms are provided free of charge. Please return yours to the stores manager when you leave.\"","item":"Return your uniform to the ___ (NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS)","answer":"stores manager","why":{"en":"Two words from the text; \"the\" is already printed.","tr":"Metinden iki kelime; \"the\" zaten yazılı.","fa":"دو کلمه از متن؛ «the» از قبل چاپ شده."}}},{"id":"GT2-career","ctx":["GT2-career"],"title":{"en":"Job and career guides","tr":"İş ve kariyer rehberleri","fa":"راهنمای کار و مسیر شغلی"},"asks":{"en":"Guides for job seekers and employees: CVs, interviews, promotion, resigning, freelance work, apprenticeships. Sentence and note completion test the advice.","tr":"İş arayanlar ve çalışanlar için rehberler: özgeçmiş, mülakat, terfi, istifa, serbest çalışma, çıraklık. Cümle ve not tamamlama tavsiyeleri sınar.","fa":"راهنما برای کارجوها و کارمندها: رزومه، مصاحبه، ترفیع، استعفا، کار آزاد، کارآموزی حرفه‌ای. کامل کردن جمله و یادداشت توصیه‌ها را می‌سنجد."},"fields":["Keep your CV to ___ pages.","Research the company before the ___.","Give your employer written ___ when you resign.","Freelancers must keep records for ___."],"words":[{"a":"CV","b":"career summary / résumé","tr":"özgeçmiş","fa":"رزومه"},{"a":"applicant","b":"candidate / person applying","tr":"başvuran","fa":"متقاضی"},{"a":"vacancy","b":"an open job","tr":"açık pozisyon","fa":"موقعیت شغلی خالی"},{"a":"interview","b":"meeting with the employer","tr":"mülakat","fa":"مصاحبه"},{"a":"resign","b":"leave your job / hand in your notice","tr":"istifa etmek","fa":"استعفا دادن"},{"a":"notice period","b":"time between resigning and leaving","tr":"ihbar süresi","fa":"مدت اطلاع قبلی"},{"a":"promotion","b":"moving up to a higher job","tr":"terfi","fa":"ترفیع"},{"a":"freelance","b":"self-employed / working for yourself","tr":"serbest","fa":"آزادکار"},{"a":"apprenticeship","b":"training while you work","tr":"çıraklık","fa":"کارآموزی حرفه‌ای"},{"a":"references","b":"people who will recommend you","tr":"referanslar","fa":"معرف‌ها"},{"a":"salary","b":"pay / earnings","tr":"maaş","fa":"حقوق"},{"a":"recent","b":"latest / most up to date","tr":"en son","fa":"جدیدترین"}],"traps":[{"en":"Advice for different stages: \"before the interview\" and \"after the interview\" are different paragraphs.","tr":"Farklı aşamalar için tavsiyeler: \"mülakattan önce\" ve \"mülakattan sonra\" farklı paragraflardadır.","fa":"توصیه برای مرحله‌های مختلف: «قبل از مصاحبه» و «بعد از مصاحبه» در پاراگراف‌های جدا هستند."},{"en":"The gap needs a word from the text, even if a synonym feels more natural.","tr":"Boşluk metinden bir kelime ister; eş anlamlısı daha doğal gelse bile.","fa":"جای خالی کلمه‌ای از متن را می‌خواهد، حتی اگر مترادفش طبیعی‌تر به نظر برسد."}],"example":{"text":"Most employers spend less than a minute on each CV, so keep yours to two pages and put your most recent job first.","item":"Sentence: Put your most ___ job first.   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"recent","why":{"en":"\"Put your most recent job first.\" Copy recent; do not change it to \"latest\".","tr":"\"En son işini en başa koy.\" recent kelimesini kopyala; \"latest\" diye değiştirme.","fa":"«جدیدترین شغلت را اول بنویس». کلمه‌ی recent را کپی کن؛ به latest تغییرش نده."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT2-career"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-career","n":18,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT2-policy","ctx":["GT2-policy"],"title":{"en":"Workplace policies and conditions","tr":"İş yeri politikaları ve çalışma koşulları","fa":"سیاست‌ها و شرایط محیط کار"},"asks":{"en":"A page from a staff handbook: parking, dress code, leave, absence, benefits or the complaints procedure. Questions test what staff must do, by when, and who they tell.","tr":"Bir personel el kitabından bir sayfa: otopark, kıyafet kuralı, izin, devamsızlık, yan haklar ya da şikâyet prosedürü. Sorular personelin ne yapması gerektiğini, ne zamana kadar ve kime haber vereceğini sınar.","fa":"صفحه‌ای از راهنمای کارکنان: پارکینگ، قانون پوشش، مرخصی، غیبت، مزایا یا روند رسیدگی به شکایت. سؤال‌ها می‌سنجند کارکنان چه باید بکنند، تا کی و به چه کسی خبر بدهند."},"fields":["Staff must inform their ___ before 9 a.m. if they are ill.","Holiday requests need ___ weeks’ notice.","Parking permits are issued by ___.","Jeans may be worn on ___."],"words":[{"a":"entitled to","b":"have the right to","tr":"... hakkı olmak","fa":"حق داشتن"},{"a":"annual leave","b":"holiday","tr":"yıllık izin","fa":"مرخصی سالانه"},{"a":"notice","b":"warning in advance","tr":"önceden haber","fa":"اطلاع قبلی"},{"a":"sick leave","b":"time off when you are ill","tr":"hastalık izni","fa":"مرخصی استعلاجی"},{"a":"permit","b":"an official permission card","tr":"izin kartı","fa":"مجوز"},{"a":"dress code","b":"rules about clothes","tr":"kıyafet kuralları","fa":"قانون پوشش"},{"a":"casual","b":"informal / relaxed","tr":"rahat, gündelik","fa":"غیررسمی"},{"a":"grievance","b":"a formal complaint","tr":"resmî şikâyet","fa":"شکایت رسمی"},{"a":"approve","b":"agree to / sign off","tr":"onaylamak","fa":"تأیید کردن"},{"a":"allowance","b":"money paid for something","tr":"ödenek","fa":"کمک‌هزینه"},{"a":"probation","b":"a trial period","tr":"deneme süresi","fa":"دوره‌ی آزمایشی"},{"a":"in writing","b":"by email or letter","tr":"yazılı olarak","fa":"به‌صورت کتبی"}],"traps":[{"en":"Who to tell: \"your line manager\" and \"HR\" are often named for different steps.","tr":"Kime haber verilir: \"bağlı olduğun yönetici\" ve \"İK\" çoğu zaman farklı adımlar için geçer.","fa":"به چه کسی خبر بدهی: «مدیر مستقیم» و «منابع انسانی» اغلب برای مرحله‌های مختلف نام برده می‌شوند."},{"en":"Periods: \"two weeks’ notice\" and \"within two weeks\" mean different things.","tr":"Süreler: \"iki hafta önceden haber\" ile \"iki hafta içinde\" farklı şeylerdir.","fa":"مدت‌ها: «دو هفته اطلاع قبلی» با «ظرف دو هفته» فرق دارد."}],"example":{"text":"If you cannot come to work because of illness, phone your line manager before 9 a.m. on the first day. HR only needs to be told if the absence lasts more than five working days.","item":"Staff who are ill must first contact their ___.   (NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS)","answer":"line manager","why":{"en":"The line manager is told first; HR only after five working days.","tr":"Önce bağlı olunan yöneticiye haber verilir; İK’ya ancak beş iş gününden sonra.","fa":"اول به مدیر مستقیم خبر می‌دهی؛ به منابع انسانی فقط بعد از پنج روز کاری."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT2-policy"],"often":{"pattern":"GT2-policy","n":11,"of":55,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 11 of the last 55 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 55 metnin 11’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۱ متن از ۵۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"A table, then a flow-chart","tr":"Bir tablo, sonra bir akış şeması","fa":"یک جدول، بعد یک فلوچارت"},"body":{"en":"Questions 15-21 are a table about the first text: ONE WORD ONLY. Questions 22-27 are a flow-chart about the second text: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. Both follow the order of their text.","tr":"Soru 15-21 ilk metinle ilgili bir tablo: ONE WORD ONLY. Soru 22-27 ikinci metinle ilgili bir akış şeması: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. İkisi de kendi metninin sırasını izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱۵ تا ۲۱ جدولی درباره‌ی متن اول‌اند: ONE WORD ONLY. سؤال‌های ۲۲ تا ۲۷ فلوچارتی درباره‌ی متن دوم‌اند: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. هر دو ترتیب متن خودشان را دنبال می‌کنند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Use the headings and the order","tr":"Başlıkları ve sırayı kullan","fa":"از عنوان‌ها و ترتیب استفاده کن"},"steps":[{"en":"Match each row of the table to a heading in the text: Pay, Holiday, Safety.","tr":"Tablonun her satırını metindeki bir başlıkla eşleştir: Pay, Holiday, Safety.","fa":"هر ردیف جدول را به یکی از عنوان‌های متن وصل کن: Pay، Holiday، Safety."},{"en":"In a flow-chart, look for order words in the text: first, next, once, then, when.","tr":"Akış şemasında metindeki sıra kelimelerini ara: first, next, once, then, when.","fa":"در فلوچارت دنبال کلمه‌های ترتیب در متن بگرد: first، next، once، then، when."},{"en":"Copy the words exactly and count them. A plural in the text stays plural.","tr":"Kelimeleri aynen kopyala ve say. Metindeki çoğul, çoğul kalır.","fa":"کلمه‌ها را دقیقاً کپی کن و بشمار. جمعِ متن جمع می‌ماند."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Count every word","tr":"Her kelimeyi say","fa":"همه‌ی کلمه‌ها را بشمار"},"body":{"en":"Two words means two: \"store manager\" is fine, \"your store manager\" is not. Articles and possessives count as words. If the printed words already include \"the\" or \"your\", do not add them again.","tr":"İki kelime iki demektir: \"store manager\" olur, \"your store manager\" olmaz. Artikeller ve iyelik sözcükleri de kelime sayılır. Yazılı kısımda zaten \"the\" ya da \"your\" varsa onları tekrar ekleme.","fa":"دو کلمه یعنی دو: «store manager» درست است، «your store manager» نه. حرف تعریف و ضمیر ملکی هم کلمه حساب می‌شوند. اگر بخش چاپ‌شده «the» یا «your» را دارد، دوباره اضافه‌شان نکن."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One flow-chart step, step by step","tr":"Bir akış şeması adımı, adım adım","fa":"یک مرحله‌ی فلوچارت، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the flow-chart. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer.","text":"\"After your interview, the agency will check your references. When these have been received, you will be offered a trial shift.\"","item":"Interview → agency checks your ___ → trial shift","answer":"references","walk":[{"en":"The step comes after the interview and before the trial shift.","tr":"Adım görüşmeden sonra, deneme vardiyasından önce geliyor.","fa":"این قدم بعد از مصاحبه و قبل از شیفت آزمایشی است."},{"en":"\"Will check your references\" matches \"agency checks your\".","tr":"\"Will check your references\", \"agency checks your\" ile eşleşiyor.","fa":"«will check your references» با «agency checks your» جور است."},{"en":"\"your\" is printed, so write one word: references.","tr":"\"your\" yazılı, tek kelime yaz: references.","fa":"«your» چاپ شده، پس یک کلمه بنویس: references."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Flow-chart gap, NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS: \"Send the form to ___\". The text says \"Send the completed form to the payroll office.\" What do you write?","options":["the payroll office","payroll office","completed form"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"the payroll office\" is three words. Two words name the place: payroll office.","tr":"\"the payroll office\" üç kelime. Yeri iki kelime söylüyor: payroll office.","fa":"«the payroll office» سه کلمه است. دو کلمه مکان را می‌گوید: payroll office."}},"remember":{"en":"Find the heading or the step, copy the text’s own words, and count them against the limit.","tr":"Başlığı ya da adımı bul, metnin kendi kelimelerini kopyala ve onları sınıra göre say.","fa":"عنوان یا قدم را پیدا کن، کلمه‌های خودِ متن را کپی کن و آن‌ها را با سقف کلمه مقایسه کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x02-r2-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r2"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 2","title":{"en":"An agency and a bike scheme","tr":"Bir ajans ve bir bisiklet programı","fa":"یک آژانس و طرح دوچرخه"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT2-career","GT2-policy"],"texts":[{"title":"TempLine Recruitment: what we promise our temporary staff","kind":"agency promises","body":"Thank you for registering with TempLine. Whether you are looking for a few days' work or a long-term placement, these are the commitments we make to everyone on our books.\n\nBefore you start\nWe will invite you to a short meeting at our office, where your consultant will talk through the kind of work you want and check your right to work in this country. Please bring your passport and a recent bank statement. You will also complete a short online course on health and safety, which takes about forty minutes.\n\nYour pay\nYou will be paid weekly, every Friday, directly into your bank account, and your payslip will be emailed to you on the same day. If you think there is a mistake, contact the payroll team before the following Wednesday.\n\nHoliday\nPaid holiday starts to build up from your first day with us, even if you only work occasionally. You can check how much you have saved up at any time through the TempLine app.\n\nNew assignments\nWherever possible, we will give you at least two days' notice of a new assignment. You are free to turn down any assignment, and doing so will never affect the offers we make to you in future.\n\nSupport\nEvery worker has a named consultant who is their main contact. If a problem comes up in the evening or at the weekend, please call our out-of-hours line rather than the office number.\n\nSafety\nBefore we send anyone to a new client, a member of our team visits the client's premises to check that they are safe. If you are involved in an accident at work, however minor, you must report it to us within 24 hours."},{"title":"Pedal to Work: our bike-loan scheme","kind":"scheme guidance","body":"Pedal to Work allows employees to get a new bicycle and safety equipment through the company and pay for it in small amounts over a year. Because payments are taken before tax, most people save between a quarter and a third of the normal price.\n\nWho can join?\nThe scheme is open to all permanent employees who have completed their probation period. Temporary and agency staff are not eligible. You must also earn enough for the monthly payments to leave your pay above the national minimum wage.\n\nHow to apply\nFirst, visit a partner shop and choose your bike. The list of partner shops is on the staff website; we cannot accept bikes bought online or from other shops. You can include a helmet, lights and a lock, up to a total value of £1,500. Ask the shop for a written quotation.\n\nNext, fill in the application form on the staff website and attach the quotation. Your application must then be approved by your line manager, who will check that you are eligible and that you intend to use the bike, at least partly, for travelling to work. Approval usually takes about a week.\n\nOnce your application has been approved, the HR department will email you a hire agreement. Read it carefully, sign it and return it within fourteen days; if it is not returned in time, the application will be cancelled and you will need to start again.\n\nCollecting your bike\nWhen the shop has your bike ready, it will contact you to arrange a time to collect it. Please bring photo identification with you, as the shop cannot hand over the bike without it.\n\nPaying for your bike\nThe cost is spread over twelve months and taken from your monthly salary, starting the month after you collect the bike. If you leave the company before the end of the year, the remaining payments will be taken from your final pay.\n\nQuestions\nThe HR team runs a short information session about the scheme on the first Monday of every month, and you can book a place through the staff website. Staff at the partner shops will also be happy to advise you on choosing the right size and type of bike for your journey."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 15-21. Complete the table below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15-21 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"table","table":{"title":"TempLine: commitments to temporary staff","headers":["Topic","Details"]},"questions":[{"n":15,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Before you start · documents to bring: your ___ and a recent bank statement","accept":["passport"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Please bring your passport and a recent bank statement","why":{"en":"\"Please bring your passport and a recent bank statement.\"","tr":"\"Lütfen pasaportunu ve yakın tarihli bir banka hesap dökümünü getir.\"","fa":"«لطفاً گذرنامه و یک صورت‌حساب بانکی جدید بیاور»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":16,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Pay · paid weekly, every ___","accept":["Friday"],"limit":1,"evidence":"every Friday, directly into your bank account","why":{"en":"\"Paid weekly, every Friday.\"","tr":"\"Haftalık, her cuma ödenir.\"","fa":"«هفتگی، هر جمعه پرداخت می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":17,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Holiday · paid holiday starts building up from your first ___","accept":["day"],"limit":1,"evidence":"starts to build up from your first day with us","why":{"en":"\"Paid holiday starts to build up from your first day with us.\"","tr":"\"Ücretli izin bizimle ilk gününden itibaren birikmeye başlar.\"","fa":"«مرخصیِ با حقوق از اولین روزی که با ما کار می‌کنی جمع می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":18,"kind":"gap","prompt":"New assignments · at least two days’ ___ whenever possible","accept":["notice"],"limit":1,"evidence":"at least two days' notice of a new assignment","why":{"en":"\"At least two days’ notice of a new assignment.\"","tr":"\"Yeni bir görev için en az iki gün önceden haber.\"","fa":"«دست‌کم دو روز اطلاع قبلی برای کار جدید»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":19,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Support · your main contact is a named ___","accept":["consultant"],"limit":1,"evidence":"Every worker has a named consultant","why":{"en":"\"Every worker has a named consultant who is their main contact.\"","tr":"\"Her çalışanın ana irtibat kişisi olan, adı belli bir danışmanı var.\"","fa":"«هر کارگر یک مشاورِ مشخص دارد که رابط اصلی‌اش است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":20,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Safety · a member of the agency checks the client’s ___","accept":["premises"],"limit":1,"evidence":"visits the client's premises to check that they are safe","why":{"en":"\"Visits the client’s premises to check that they are safe.\"","tr":"\"Güvenli olup olmadığını kontrol etmek için müşterinin iş yerini ziyaret eder.\"","fa":"«محل کار مشتری را بازدید می‌کند تا مطمئن شود امن است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":21,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Safety · report any ___ to the agency within 24 hours","accept":["accident"],"limit":1,"evidence":"If you are involved in an accident at work","why":{"en":"\"If you are involved in an accident at work, however minor, you must report it to us within 24 hours.\"","tr":"\"İşte, ne kadar küçük olursa olsun, bir kazaya karışırsan bunu 24 saat içinde bize bildirmelisin.\"","fa":"«اگر در محل کار دچار حادثه شدی، هرچقدر کوچک، باید ظرف ۲۴ ساعت به ما خبر بدهی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 22-27. Complete the flow-chart below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 22-27 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"flow-chart","flowTitle":"Joining Pedal to Work","questions":[{"n":22,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Choose a bike (and safety equipment) at a ___","accept":["partner shop"],"limit":2,"evidence":"visit a partner shop and choose your bike","why":{"en":"\"Visit a partner shop and choose your bike.\" Bikes from other shops or online are not accepted.","tr":"\"Bir anlaşmalı mağazaya git ve bisikletini seç.\" Başka mağazalardan ya da internetten alınan bisikletler kabul edilmiyor.","fa":"«به یکی از فروشگاه‌های همکار برو و دوچرخه‌ات را انتخاب کن». دوچرخه از فروشگاه‌های دیگر یا اینترنت قبول نمی‌شود."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":23,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Complete the ___ on the staff website and attach the written quotation","accept":["application form"],"limit":2,"evidence":"fill in the application form on the staff website","why":{"en":"\"Fill in the application form on the staff website and attach the quotation.\" Two words.","tr":"\"Personel web sitesindeki başvuru formunu doldur ve fiyat teklifini ekle.\" İki kelime.","fa":"«فرم درخواست را در وب‌سایت کارکنان پر کن و پیش‌فاکتور را پیوست کن». دو کلمه."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":24,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Your ___ checks that you are eligible and approves the application","accept":["line manager"],"limit":2,"evidence":"approved by your line manager","why":{"en":"\"Approved by your line manager\". \"your\" is printed: write two words.","tr":"\"Bağlı olduğun yönetici tarafından onaylanır\". \"your\" yazılı: iki kelime yaz.","fa":"«توسط مدیر مستقیمت تأیید می‌شود». «your» چاپ شده: دو کلمه بنویس."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":25,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Sign the ___ from HR and return it within fourteen days","accept":["hire agreement"],"limit":2,"evidence":"will email you a hire agreement","why":{"en":"\"The HR department will email you a hire agreement. Read it carefully, sign it and return it within fourteen days.\"","tr":"\"İK departmanı sana bir kiralama sözleşmesi e-postayla gönderir. Dikkatle oku, imzala ve on dört gün içinde geri gönder.\"","fa":"«بخش منابع انسانی یک قرارداد اجاره برایت ایمیل می‌کند. با دقت بخوان، امضا کن و ظرف چهارده روز برگردان»."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":26,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Collect the bike from the shop and show ___","accept":["photo identification"],"limit":2,"evidence":"Please bring photo identification with you","why":{"en":"\"Please bring photo identification with you\": the shop will not hand over the bike without it.","tr":"\"Lütfen yanında fotoğraflı kimlik getir\": mağaza bisikleti onsuz teslim etmez.","fa":"«لطفاً کارت شناسایی عکس‌دار همراهت بیاور»: فروشگاه بدون آن دوچرخه را تحویل نمی‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-limit","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":27,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Twelve payments are taken from your ___","accept":["monthly salary"],"limit":2,"evidence":"taken from your monthly salary","why":{"en":"\"Spread over twelve months and taken from your monthly salary\".","tr":"\"On iki aya yayılır ve aylık maaşından kesilir\".","fa":"«در دوازده ماه تقسیم و از حقوق ماهانه‌ات کم می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x02-r2-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r2"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"She turned down the offer of extra shifts.\" \"Turned down\" means...","options":["refused","accepted","reduced"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"To turn down an offer = to say no to it.","tr":"Bir teklifi turn down etmek = ona hayır demek.","fa":"turn down کردنِ پیشنهاد یعنی نه گفتن به آن."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"Which phrase means \"staff who are allowed to join\"?","options":["temporary staff","senior staff","eligible staff"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Eligible = allowed to take part.","tr":"Eligible = katılmaya hakkı olan.","fa":"eligible یعنی مجاز به شرکت."}},{"tests":"method","point":3,"prompt":"NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. Gap: \"Return the agreement to ___\". The text says \"Return the signed agreement to the HR department.\" What do you write?","options":["the HR department","HR department","signed agreement"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"the HR department\" is three words; two words name the place.","tr":"\"the HR department\" üç kelime; yeri iki kelime söylüyor.","fa":"«the HR department» سه کلمه است؛ دو کلمه مکان را می‌گوید."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"ONE WORD ONLY. Table: \"lockers are checked every ___\". The text says \"Lockers are checked on the last Friday of each month.\" What do you write?","options":["month","Friday","fortnight"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Every ___\" + \"the last Friday of each month\" = every month. Friday alone would mean every week.","tr":"\"Every ___\" + \"her ayın son cuması\" = her ay. Yalnızca Friday her hafta anlamına gelirdi.","fa":"«every ___» + «آخرین جمعه‌ی هر ماه» یعنی هر ماه. فقط Friday یعنی هر هفته."}}],"id":"c-x02-r2-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r2"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
